      "sentence_id": 1,
      "japanese": "ジョン・バーニンガム作『おじいちゃん』表紙絵本は小さな子どもがお母さんに読んでもらうものだ、と思う人も多いかもしれません。",
      "english_translation": "Many people might think that the picture book version of \"Grandpa\" by John Burningham, intended for young children to read with their mothers, is a simple and straightforward story."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 2,
      "japanese": "でも、絵本の中には、みなさんが読んでもおもしろいものがたくさんあります。",
      "english_translation": "However, there are many interesting things in picture books that you will find enjoyable to read."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 3,
      "japanese": "ウソだと思う人は、大きな本屋の絵本コーナーや図書館の絵本コーナーに行ってみてください。",
      "english_translation": "If you don't believe me, please go to the picture book section in a large bookstore or at a library."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 4,
      "japanese": "たくさんある絵本の中には、読んでみようと思う絵本があるはずです。",
      "english_translation": "There must be many picture books, and I'm sure there's at least one that I want to read."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "japanese": "それらの絵本を、5冊くらい読んでみましょう。",
      "english_translation": "Let's read about five of those books."
    }
